# Build context is the repo root (see apps/api/Dockerfile), so this keeps the context small and,
# more importantly, keeps secrets and local state out of the image.
node_modules
**/node_modules

# Secrets and backups. deploy/.env holds every password; a backup in the image would be a database
# copy shipped to wherever the image goes.
deploy/.env
deploy/backups

# Build output of the DELETED React console. Nothing produces this any more, but a developer whose
# tree predates the removal still has it on disk — and with the console build stage gone, `COPY
# apps/api` would bake 264 KB of unreachable JavaScript into their image with nothing saying so. It
# was gitignored, which kept it out of commits and did nothing about the build context.
apps/api/public/app

# Local agent/vector state — machine-specific, regenerated, never a build input.
.claude-flow
.swarm
ruvector.db
agentdb.rvf
agentdb.rvf.lock

.git
.github
docs
spikes
**/test
*.md
*.html

# …except the console. The `*.html` line above is aimed at the docs and handoff pages at the repo
# root, and it silently swallowed the web console's shell as well — the image built cleanly and
# served a 404 for `/`. Negations are evaluated in order, so this must stay BELOW that rule.
!apps/api/public/*.html

# The design source, and the one file in it that must never ship.
#
# `Farm_app_design_exploration/ref/panel-x1pro.png` is a REAL SCREEN CAPTURE. It exists so the
# device frames could be designed against real pixels, and it is a stand-in — inside a frame, the
# only thing that may ever appear is the live framebuffer. A screenshot dressed as a running device
# is the exact lie the whole frame system is built to avoid.
#
# The `*.html` rule above matches root-level files ONLY, so the `.dc.html` documents and this
# capture would both be copied into the image the moment somebody commits the folder. Nothing
# references them today; this is what stops that changing quietly.
Farm_app_design_exploration
